<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.4.1: Comparing Scatter Plots with Linear and Nonlinear Trends</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00754</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.4.1: Comparing Scatter Plots with Linear and Nonlinear Trends</md:title>
    <md:uuid>486fae87-6225-4c5a-927a-076f5e4b30ea</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <para>Which one doesn’t belong?</para>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>A.
            <media
              alt="Graph of a scatter plot, origin O. distance (miles) and cost (dollars).">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_02_01.svg" />
            </media>
            </para>
          <para>B.
            <media
              alt="Graph of a scatter plot, origin O, with grid. Height (millimeters) and weight (milligrams).">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_02_02.svg" />
            </media>
            </para>
          <para>C.
            <media alt="A scatterplot.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_02_03.svg" />
            </media>
            </para>
          <para>D.<media alt="A scatterplot.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_02_04.svg" />
            </media>
            </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
          <para>A doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that fit a line well
            and are increasing.</para>
          <para>B doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that would not fit a
            line well and do not show a pattern.</para>
          <para>C doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that would fit a line
            well and are decreasing.</para>
          <para>D doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that would not fit a
            line well and do show a curved pattern.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>
  </content>
